1.1.3
The replication portfolio
In a complete market, every contingent claim can be replicated with a trading strategy, or replicating portfolio, made
of the underlying asset X and a risk-free money account. For instance, Black and Scholes derived the price of an
option by constructing a replicating portfolio (see details in Section (1.2.2)). As discussed above, this is not the case in
an incomplete market. We are brieﬂy going to introduce the theory of portfolio replication in complete and incomplete
markets (details can be found in Oksendal [1998], Shreve [2004], Cont et al.
[2003]). We let (X(t))t∈[0,T ] be a
