maturity direction. However, Roper assumed that the total variance was twice differentiable in the strike direction.
This regularity is certainly not required. Guo et al. [2012] showed that by starting from option prices convex in K,
their ﬁrst derivative are deﬁned almost everywhere, and so are those of the total variance (in K or η), since the BlackScholes mapping in total variance is smooth. As a result, one can assume that for any t, the function k →w(η, t) is
continuous and almost everywhere differentiable.
In addition, some other asymptotic behaviours of d1 and d2 hold in great generality. For instance, the SmallMoneyness Behaviour (SMB) condition, proved by Rogers et al. [2010], states
lim
η→−∞d2(η, ω(η, t)) = ∞
(1.4.22)
Further, Rogers et al. [2010] imposed two further constraints on the LMB and SMB, obtaining the following Lemma:
Lemma 1.4.1 Let ω be any positive real function. Then
lim
η→∞d2(η, ω(η)) = −∞
lim
η→−∞d1(η, ω(η)) = ∞
Equivalently, using Equation (1.4.22), Guo et al. [2012] showed that the marginal law of the stock price at some ﬁxed
time t > 0 has no mass at zero if and only if
lim
K→0 ∂KC(K, t) = −P(0, t)
(1.4.23)
