1.4.4.2
Iterative methods
Even though there exists different iterative methods taking an initial estimate, or interval of estimates, to infer the
implied volatility, the ﬁnancial industry favours the Newton-Raphson method (see Chriss [1997]). Chance et al.
[2014] showed that computational considerations, such as the tolerence level and the initial input, have a signiﬁcant
inﬂuence on the existence and shape of the volatility smile. When we let the Black-Scholes volatility in Equation
(1.2.6) tends respectively to zero and inﬁnity, we get the limits
