that unique probability measure equivalent to P is such that the discounted stock price plus the cumulated dividends
are martingale when the riskless asset is the numeraire. There are various ways of modelling discrete dividends, all
resulting in different prices for path dependent options (see Appendix (B.2)). In a general setting, we let the underlying
process (Sx
