where δ(.) is the Dirac function. In general, in low dimensions, those expectations are solved numerically by diffusing
forward the joint distributions of the underlying asset and the arbitrary variables (see Jex et al. [1999]).
1.7.2.2
The local volatility of the underlying with deterministic rates
Assuming deterministic rates, Dupire [1996] deﬁned the local variance (LV) as the expectation of the future spot
variance conditional on a given asset price level. More speciﬁcally, given the dynamics of the underlying process in
Section (1.7.1) with deterministic interest rates, and applying Gyongy’s results, we get
d ˜St
