• when α ≤1, then E[|X|] = +∞and the mean of X is undeﬁned.
• when 1 < α ≤2, then E[|X|] < ∞and the mean of X is deﬁned.
• when 0 < α < 2, then E[|X|2] = E[X2] = +∞and stable distributions do not have ﬁnite second moments
(variances).
