that is, X = αZI{Y =1} +βZI{Y =0}. From independence we get E[ZI{f(Y )}] = E[Z]E[I{f(Y )}], such that E[X] =
0. The standard deviation α and β must be chosen such that the variance of X is 1, that is,
V ar(X) = E[X2] = pα2 + (1 −p)β2 = 1
