6.1.2
The parametric models
Using parametric representations of the market prices, proper option portfolio management requires suitably chosen
interpolation and extrapolation techniques of the IV surface, forcing practitioners to use a fully speciﬁed model. The
standard approach is to interpolate and extrapolate market prices, or volatilities, to complete the market. Practitioners
use the Black-Scholes implied volatility and smooth the prices in a parabolic way to generate the missing prices. Due
to the difﬁculty of deﬁning a single parametric function for the entire volatility surface, a typical solution is to estimate
each smile independently with some nonlinear function. Then, the IV surface is reconstructed by interpolating total
variances along the forward moneyness.
6.1.2.1
The polynomial models
