by Malz [1997], and to cut the volatility outside that region. Similarly, Daglish et al.
[2006] performed a Taylor
expansion up to the second order of the implied volatility surface around the money forward level. In general, the
implied volatility is modelled with a functional form of the smile around the money forward as follow:
