6.2.3.2
Example of term structure
We are now going to test the capacity of different models to generate term structutre of volatility reaching the steepest
possible down hump in a no-arbitrage setup. We constrain the initial volatility to be s0 = 0.35 and the inﬁnite volatility
to be s∞= 0.15, and we calibrate the models to reach a minimum at the earliest possible maturity. We test the Heston
model, the Gurrieri model, and Expo2 and Expo3 models with settings given in Table ( 6.1). For the Heston model
the inﬁnite variance is θ = 0.0225 and the speed of mean reversion is κ = 72, while for the Gurrieri model we get
B = −3.5 and the speed of mean reversion is κ = 30, leading to τ = 1
κ = 0.033, with a no-arbitrage constraint of
0.0042. We show the results in Figure ( 6.3) and display a zoom in Figure ( 6.4) for maturities in the range [0, 0.1].
